[Mission1.Objectives]
Push the enemy out of the town.
[Mission1.Description]
There is a small group of Germans in the town ahead. The enemy is not aware of our presence so we must attack quickly and decisively in order to drive them out.

Your orders:
-	Liberate the town from the Germans.
[Mission1.Success]
Order carried out, the enemy is defeated and the town liberated! The Allied offensive can now continue.
[Mission1.Failed]
Mission failed! Your troops were eliminated! This defeat will make the rest of the operation a lot harder.
[Submission2.Objectives]
Repulse the German attack.
[Submission2.Description]
The situation is critical! The Germans have brought up their reserves in the operation area. German units have forced a break-through and are moving toward our positions in town in order to push us out.

Your orders: 
-	Consolidate your positions and repulse the advancing enemy forces.
[Submission2.Success]
Order carried out! The enemy attack has been repulsed. Good job!
[Submission2.Failed]
Mission failed! Your troops have been driven away from the town. Your failure threatens the very success of the entire operation!
[StringTable.Reserv]
Reinforcements have arrived.
[StringTable.Subtitle_01]
France. June 1944